<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Karnataka</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Karnataka is a state of south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, with its capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bengaluru">Bengaluru</a> and a mainly Kannada-speaking population. It was the heartland of dynasties including the Kadambas, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-ganga-dynasty">Western Gangas</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chalukya-dynasty">Chalukyas</a>, Rashtrakutas, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hoysala-empire">Hoysalas</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vijayanagara-empire">Vijayanagara Empire</a>, and later of the Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mysore">Mysore</a>. The state was formed as Mysore State in 1956 by uniting the Kannada-speaking areas and was renamed Karnataka in 1973.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/karnataka.jpg" alt="Karnataka" width="320" height="175" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Apadegal · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hampi_virupaksha_temple.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
